  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;The proposed development by reason of its failure to provide appropriate horizontal stacking for the double bedroom at Flat D and the inadequate internal floorspace for proposed Flat B would cumulatively result in sub-standard level of living accommodation for future occupiers of the proposed flats., to the detriment of their residential amenity.&amp;nbsp; The proposed development is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 D.7 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policies DM1 and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Residential Design Guide SPD (2010).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;The proposed on-site parking arrangement, by reason of failure to demonstrate that the proposed development would provide a lawful and safe vehicular access to all the proposed car parking spaces would have an adverse impact on the safe access to the site from the public highway. The proposal would therefore be detrimental to highway safety, contrary to Policy T4,&amp;nbsp; of the London Plan (2021) and Policies DM26 and DM42 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;The proposed external alterations to provide a single entrance door would appear out of character with the existing streetscene appearing as an incongruous feature in the locality. Furthermore, the proposed subdivision of the rear amenity space would visually break up the garden space and create unnecessary compact spaces which would break up the well spaced pattern of rear gardens, contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 D.1, D.11 of the London Plan (2021), Policies DM1 and DM27 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), Core Policy CS.1B of the Harrow Core Strategy and the Residential Design Guide SPD (2010).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
